content:
{
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent sample size: synopsis states 590 patients randomized, but population section says 590 projected after SCC enrollment, and 460 SCC randomized",
      "page": 27,
      "quote": "Approximately 590 patients will be randomized to either the experimental cemiplimab treatment arm or the IC of chemotherapy control treatment arm.",
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "title": "Contradictory enrollment criteria: target population says only squamous histology enrolled starting Amendment 5, but objectives and statistical plan include all eligible histologies (SCC and AC)",
      "page": 29,
      "quote": "Starting with Amendment 5, only patients with squamous histology will be enrolled.",
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent number of IC chemotherapy options: text says 4 classes but lists 5 drugs (pemetrexed, topotecan, irinotecan, gemcitabine, vinorelbine)",
      "page": 27,
      "quote": "IC chemotherapy options are 4 classes: (1) antifolate - pemetrexed, (2) topoisomerase 1 inhibitor - topotecan or irinotecan, (3) nucleoside analogue – gemcitabine, and (4) vinca alkaloid - vinorelbine.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Interim analysis timing contradicts study design: synopsis says second interim analysis demonstrated survival advantage, but statistical plan says two interim analyses planned at 70% and 85% events",
      "page": 28,
      "quote": "The second interim analysis demonstrated survival advantage for patients treated with cemiplimab over IC chemotherapy.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Missing primary endpoint analysis for overall population: statistical plan says OS tested in SCC first, then overall, but no details on overall population analysis or sample size/power",
      "page": 30,
      "quote": "If the null hypothesis is rejected in the SCC patients, then OS will be tested in the overall population.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent treatment duration: synopsis says treatment period up to 96 weeks (16 cycles of 6 weeks), but cemiplimab is Q3W, so 96 weeks would be 32 cycles, not 16",
      "page": 28,
      "quote": "Cycle length is 6 weeks, and tumor imaging is planned to be conducted on day 42 (±7 days) of cycles 1–4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, and 16. Planned treatment is for up to 96 weeks.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent cycle length for Q3W regimens: cemiplimab and most chemotherapies are Q3W, but cycle length defined as 6 weeks",
      "page": 28,
      "quote": "Cycle length is 6 weeks",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Missing analysis for DOR endpoint: DOR listed as secondary endpoint but no statistical analysis described",
      "page": 29,
      "quote": "Other secondary endpoints will include DOR, QOL, and the safety and tolerability of cemiplimab.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent alpha spending: first interim at 70% events (238/340) but second at 85% (289/340) – 85% of 340 is 289, but 70% is 238, which is correct; however, the text says 70% and 85% but the first interim is at 70% and second at 85%, which is fine; but the nominal alphas (0.0074, 0.0129, 0.0202) sum to 0.0405, exceeding the overall 0.025 one-sided",
      "page": 30,
      "quote": "The first interim efficacy analysis will be performed after observing approximately 238 OS events (70% of total OS events). It is projected that an observed HR of 0.729 or lower would result in a statistically significant improvement in OS at the 1-sided nominal type I error of 0.0074 at the first interim efficacy analysis. The second interim efficacy analysis will be performed after observing approximately 289 OS events (85% of total OS events). It is projected that an observed HR of 0.769 or lower would result in a statistically significant improvement in OS at the 1-sided nominal type I error of 0.0129 at the second interim efficacy analysis. The final efficacy analysis will be performed after observing approximately 340 OS events. It is projected that an observed HR of 0.801 or lower would result in a statistically significant improvement in OS at the 1-sided nominal type I error of 0.0202 at the final analysis.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent statement about retreatment: synopsis says retreatment no longer an option, but introduction describes a patient who resumed cemiplimab after progression",
      "page": 28,
      "quote": "Retreatment is no longer an option as of Amendment 7.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Missing reference to Section 7.1.7.1: cross-reference to a section not present in the excerpt (table of contents does not list section 7.1.7.1)",
      "page": 28,
      "quote": "provide they meet criteria per Section 7.1.7.1",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent abbreviation: EORTC QLQ-C30 is defined as 'European Organization for Research and Treatment of Cancer Quality of Life Questionnaire-Core 30' but abbreviation list says 'EORTC QLQ30'",
      "page": 27,
      "quote": "European Organization for Research and Treatment of Cancer Quality of Life Questionnaire-Core 30 (EORTC QLQ-C30)",
      "severity": "minor"
    }
  ]
}
